v2.0 (2026-07-25)
-----------------
- Rewrite the dashboard in Python with FastAPI and Jinja2, replacing the
  Sinatra application, and keep the URL layout so that existing bookmarks work.
- Remove the bundled jQuery, Bootstrap and DataTables assets and the Ruby
  runtime, Gemfile and Rakefile with them. Pico.css and Grid.js replace them,
  and there is no build step and no Node.js dependency.
- Read settings from FINANCE_DASHBOARD_ environment variables first and
  config.yml second, replacing .config.yml.
- Enable Basic authentication only when a user name and a password or its
  SHA-256 digest are configured, covering the data files as well as the pages.
- Keep the recently viewed codes in a signed session cookie instead of a
  database, and remove config/database.yml.
- Cache each data file by modification time and size, so a file the pipeline
  regenerates is picked up without restarting the service.
- Add etc/finance-dashboard.service, and rewrite deploy.sh to refresh a virtual
  environment and restart the unit instead of deploying the Sinatra tree.
- Add the pytest suite under test/, which builds its own data directory and
  never reads the configured one.
- Add pyproject.toml, doc/LICENSE, doc/COPYING and doc/COPYING.LESSER,
  declaring the dual GPLv3 or LGPLv3 license.

Before v2.0
-----------
- The repository carries no release tag and no version file for any revision
  before v2.0, so no earlier version number is recorded here. The Sinatra era
  survives as a numbered commit series ending at "157 Fix Quick link"
  (2019-10-17), and the commit log is its only history. Nothing has been
  reconstructed from it into a version entry.

Version History Guidelines
==========================
- Write one coherent change per physical line, as a rule.
- Keep entries near 100 columns where practical. Necessary file names,
  command names, option names, and configuration names may extend an entry
  to approximately 120 columns.
- When a version history already exists, balance a new entry against the
  length of the existing lines, so that the whole file stays consistent.
- When an entry becomes substantially longer, omit or abstract implementation
  details, examples, reasons, and secondary effects where possible.
- Preserve the changed target, externally observable behavior, compatibility
  or security impact, and important option or configuration names.
- Combine related changes within the same version, especially changes to the
  same file or feature.
- Place closely related entries near each other.
- Append an independent new change to the end of the current version entry.
- This file records the history of the repository. The Version History block in
  a module header records the history of that file, and the two are kept apart:
  a release entry here does not raise a module version, and a module version
  does not become an entry here unless the change is observable from outside.
- A change to how a generated file is parsed is recorded here and in
  doc/DATA_CONTRACT.md in the same commit, because the summary files are read
  positionally and a silent divergence from the producing side is what that
  document exists to prevent.
